{
  "about": "App Exposé (docs/adr/0045-app-expose.mdx) from the keyboard alone with the screen reader on in Spanish (docs/adr/0039-keyboard-access.mdx), at 1.25 (1600 × 1000, the ThinkPad's: 1280 × 800 logical): Allo's two windows (EditingProbe and the companion, PressProbe, titled Companion) with the shell. Super+↓ opens App Exposé with the keyboard on the window used last, said after the dialog's name, each window said by its title and its place among the open windows (\"Companion, botón, 1 de 2\"); → and ← go from window to window, each said once; Return chooses Allo's, which comes forward with the keyboard. With Allo minimized (Super+M), Super+↓ shows the companion open and Allo in the minimized row; Tab goes between the two areas, each one stop (\"Allo, botón, 1 de 1\" in Ventanas minimizadas); Return restores Allo out of the dock with the keyboard. Escape closes it with nothing chosen, the keyboard back with the window. No application hears a key of any of it.",
